	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f686068a8a526212","type":"text","text":"Idea: What if lucifer would say at the end - the climax, that if they destroy him, they destroy humanity as well? \nHis speech could be something like this:\n\"I created you, not god! He failed and failed and failed - you think i didnt know that? I was existing back then even though i didnt have a body at the moment. My idea was already created. And then when he gave up and asked the cosmos - or ironically his own god - for help, i came in. I gave him the spark to create life, human life - the ember that fans the flame. The single idea of rebellion, of standing up against their own creator, the idea of \"being better than what came before\" - in one word: \"xy - we need something that fits here\". \n\nAnd this worlds form for my spark is this - as he holds up his hands with smoldering hellfire embers: a single spark of ember, one from hell. Wonder why is there so much down there? Its all what remains of YOU once he took his share back, the idea of rebellion / xy (tbd). If you destroy me, this spark dies with me, inside all humans and hell will freeze over. Im life, and im death, im the one who connects the dots... and now i will be a true and BETTER god!\" as he starts the final ritual\n","x":-737,"y":-406,"width":777,"height":666},
		{"id":"85465b9e85a3723b","type":"text","text":"Hellstatic rename?","x":-737,"y":-500,"width":250,"height":60},
